sn3.15:6.1 | S: Then, understanding this matter, on that occasion the Buddha recited these verses: | T: Then, on realizing the significance of that, the Blessed One on that occasion exclaimed:
sn3.15:7.1 | S: “A man goes on plundering | T: “A man may plunder
sn3.15:7.2 | S: as long as it serves his ends. | T: as long as it serves his ends,
sn3.15:7.3 | S: But as soon as others plunder him, | T: but when others are plundered,
sn3.15:7.4 | S: the plunderer is plundered. | T: he who has plundered gets plundered in turn.
sn3.15:8.1 | S: For the fool thinks they’re on solid ground, | T: A fool thinks, ‘Now’s my chance,’
sn3.15:8.2 | S: so long as their wickedness has not ripened. | T: as long as his evil has yet to ripen.
sn3.15:8.3 | S: But as soon as that wickedness ripens, | T: But when it ripens,
sn3.15:8.4 | S: they fall into suffering. | T: the fool falls into pain.
sn3.15:9.1 | S: A killer creates a killer; | T: Killing, you gain your killer.
sn3.15:9.2 | S: a conqueror creates a conqueror; | T: Conquering, you gain one who will conquer you;
sn3.15:9.3 | S: an abuser creates abuse, | T: insulting, insult;
sn3.15:9.4 | S: and a bully creates a bully. | T: harassing, harassment.
sn3.15:9.5 | S: And so as deeds unfold | T: And so, through the cycle of action,
sn3.15:9.6 | S: the plunderer is plundered.” | T: he who has plundered gets plundered in turn.”


